✅ Correct fix: KEEP command.Edit(), but HIDE it
You want:

Add → works

Delete → works

Edit button → hidden

Solution: keep the Edit command but hide it with CSS.

✔ Keep your existing code (do NOT remove command.Edit)
csharp
command.Edit()
    .Text("Edit")
    .IconClass("k-icon k-i-edit")
    .HtmlAttributes(new { @class = "scparts-edit-hidden scparts-action-btn k-button" });
✔ Add CSS to hide the Edit button
html
<style>
    .scparts-edit-hidden {
        display: none !important;
    }
</style>
This keeps the Edit command in the DOM (so Telerik can generate inline editors), but hides it from the user.
